WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.950
<b>Drawing Fun!</b>

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:02.960
Drawing!

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:03.950
F - U - N !

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:06.290
Big sister Kisaragi!
 Big sister Kisaragi!

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.760
Big Sister! You're falling over!

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.020
<b>ZZZzzzzz</b>

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.250
Heavy!

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:12.290
<b> Klong</b>

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.690
Yay! Big sister is back!

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:16.900
So!

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.200
GA. Geijutsuka Art Design Class...

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:20.300
is star...

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.620
Is starting now!

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.590
She fell asleep!

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.100
Let's try to stay awake.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.480
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:57.100
<b>GA Painting Materials Storage</b>

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:57.100
What Are Little Girls Made Of?

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.810
I wonder, what are little girls made of?

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.690
What do you think? What are little girls made of?

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.170
I think they must be made

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.990
from wonderful tools 
and interesting materials.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.380
For example!

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.320
If you added clay, you'd get 
an energetic and tomboyish girl.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.350
If you added drafting tools, 
you'd get a composed and reliable girl.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:28.530
If you added a sketchbook,
 you'd get a cute and stylish girl.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.850
If you added a jar 
of oil for oil painting,

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:33.530
you'd get a slightly mysterious girl.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:37.100
All the girls that were
 born this way are in GA,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.450
Geijutsuka Art Design class,
 and learn about art

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:44.510
and design and youth, 
passing their days without worry.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.250
What do you think of my manga?

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:48.700
That's all you have?

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.250
By the way, what do you 
think Kisaragi-chan is made of?

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.060
Glasses?

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:52.690
Round glasses.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:53.540
Gotta be glasses.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:00.260
<b>Surrealism</b>

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.480
<b>This box is trash, right?</b>

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.960
<b>Isn't that the box 
and packing paper</b>

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.660
<b>that the painting and teaching
 materials were delivered in?</b>

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.380
<b>Oh! Look, look!</b>

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.080
<b>Noda-chan!</b>

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:08.900
<b>Just kidding!</b>

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:10.150
<b>Kyouju!</b>

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:12.170
<b>Then I'll be, I'll be...</b>

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.260
<b>Namiko-san!</b>

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.910
<b>Wow!</b>

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:16.770
<b>Noda, why don't you look over here for a second?</b>

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.660
A scene composed of neutral colors.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.720
Although the color scheme 
is monotonous and sharp,

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.480
it's easy on the eyes even
 after long periods of time.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.140
It is often used in office settings.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.310
A scene composed of natural colors.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.500
It is a color scheme that 
represses cold artificiality

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.370
and puts the heart at ease.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.080
Works for any setting.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.820
A scene composed of contrasting colors.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.380
Depending on its use, 
it can produce an accented

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:41.910
or lively atmosphere.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:45.390
Lastly, scenery that cannot be 
classified into any of the above.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:46.700
What?!

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:46.700
What do you mean by that?!

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.350
Hey, it's a naturally harmonious scene!

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.000
There are two methods 
by which color is classified:

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.310
“systematic color naming” and 
“characteristic color naming”.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.750
For example, b16

00:03:55.600 --> 00:04:01.750
<b><Tone Symbol>
b16
<Systematic Name>
Bright Greenish Blue
<Characteristic Name>
Light Leek Color</b>

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:59.310
The systematic name is "bright greenish blue".

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:01.420
The characteristic name is "light leek".

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.570
Bright Reddish Orange.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:07.990
<b>Bright Reddish Orange</b>

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.240
What would be the characteristic name?

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.690
Hmm...

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:07.990
Carrot?

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:10.040
Bright Yellowish Orange.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:12.260
<b>Bright Yellowish Orange</b>

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.170
The color of an egg yolk?

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:13.300
Deep Yellow.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:14.970
<b>Deep Yellow</b>

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.970
Mustard!

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:16.860
Ooh! Yeah, just like it.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.550
She's definitely just blurting out

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:20.970
the first thing that comes to mind.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:24.210
And yet, she's gotten them all right.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:26.520
What about...
do you know the difference

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:28.150
between warm and cool colors?

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.920
Man, even I know stuff like that.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:34.590
<b>Warm Color</b>

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.340
Red, orange, and other colors that

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.220
have a warming affect are warm colors.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:38.960
<b>Cool Color</b>

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:37.460
Blue, purple, and other colors that

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.960
have a cooling affect are cool colors, right?

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.830
Right, and as for us...

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.620
Tomokane and Kisaragi-chan 
are warm color types

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.800
and Kyouju and Namiko-san 
are cool color types.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:47.430
Right?

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.380
So then, which one is Noda-chan?

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.080
Hot? Cool?

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.700
If I had to pick one...

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:56.800
Lukewarm?

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.430
No, yellowish!

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.710
Ah, I thought so too!

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:02.480
She's bright and stands out.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.250
It's the color of vitamins.

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:06.170
<b> Tap tap</b>

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.270
Oh! Am I being praised?

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:08.990
In that case, I give you a 
new jersey that fits you perfectly!

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:10.990
It's black and yellow!

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.270
Oh! This will stand out even from far away.

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:17.780
Black and yellow.
 The colors indicative of caution or danger.

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:18.810
Seriously?

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:25.000
It says it's a psychological test based on colors.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.630
Noda, what's your favorite color?

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.670
Yellow, for sure.

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:30.510
But recently, I kind of like purple too.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:33.400
Yellow is happy, simple, light.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.140
<b>Happy – Simple – Light</b>

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.880
<b> High Class – Mysterious – Elegant</b>

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.350
Purple is high class, mysterious, elegant.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.890
In other words, Noda has recently had 
a desire to become more womanly.

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:41.180
Oh, I see!

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:42.520
Was it right?

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:45.320
So! So!
 Kyouju, what's your favorite color?

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.050
Black.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:47.920
Let's see, black is...

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:52.240
Silence, melancholy, suspicion.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.510
There's also worry, sin and evil.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:58.300
She already knew...

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:01.100
Let's end the psychological color test.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.280
Then, how about this one?

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:10.380
<b>Balanced between sweet and sour</b>

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.250
What's your favorite shaved ice flavor?

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:09.210
They say you can determine a person's perfect match with this test.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.420
Really?

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.650
<b>1. Ujikintoki Flavor:
 Not too sweet</b>

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:12.650
Not too sweet: Ujikintoki flavor.

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:14.820
<b>3. Cola flavor:
Explosive character</b>

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:14.820
I like Cola flavor. I usually get it.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.630
See? Your personalities are already–

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:19.090
I like attention flavor!

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:20.580
Attention flavor?!

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:23.590
Attention Flavor

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:24.930
Whoa, you guys.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.680
What are you doing playing 
with the color arrangement paper?

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:27.700
Such a waste!

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:30.090
Origami

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.160
No! It's this!

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.100
Origami?

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:31.860
Wow, how nostalgic!

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.030
Why do you have this?

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.370
They were selling it at the school supply shop.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.500
I thought it would be fun 
for everyone, so I bought it!

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:38.110
But Kisaragi-chan...

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:39.650
As soon as she touched the paper

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.940
she turned into crane-folding 
home industry girl.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:43.090
So many!

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:46.120
There's a girl like that in every class.

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:50.590
<b>whoosh   whoosh</b>

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:50.590
For some reason,
 Kyouju is only using the black paper.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:54.670
Wait, is there normally that much 
black paper in an origami packet?

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:57.600
<b>whoosh   whoosh</b>

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:57.600
Kyouju's thousand cranes will be all black!

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.220
Okay! Play time is over.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:01.900
We have to work on our
 color arrangement assignment.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:04.960
What color should we 
choose for this arrangement?

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:07.870
Maybe, a light water blue?

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:10.420
Oh! We're out of pale tone colors!

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.050
Oh, the lighter color ones right?

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:13.630
Should I lend you mine?

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:14.730
Oh, no. That's all right.

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:17.040
We have class tomorrow as well,
 so I'll go buy some.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.650
Do you know where the 
university school supply shop is?

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:21.330
Yes, more or less.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.540
It's easy to get lost if you go through the inner courtyard.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:26.050
so it might be better to enter
 through the front.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:27.160
Got it.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.580
Do you have money
 and your cell phone?

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:30.290
Yes!

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:33.020
If a stranger offers you gum,
 don't go with them!

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:33.970
Yes...

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:37.140
Also, if you get lost, find a
 landmark and call us from there!

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:39.400
Why don't you just go 
with her, mother Namiko?

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:44.410
I'm sorry.
 I ended up bringing everyone along.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:47.740
Running out of pale colors 
first is very you, Kisaragi-chan.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.540
I use up pure colors like 
yellow and orange and purple first.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:53.820
Oh, that's very Noda-chan like as well.

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:57.820
I guess, we end up using up
 colors that we like best.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:58.910
Which means that...

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:01.840
Kyouju would need... 
nothing but achromatic black.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.830
A gross, 144 packets!

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.080
Of course!

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:08.780
<b> Poster Color</b>

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:08.780
 Pigment, Water, 
and Gum arabic 
are combined 
to create this
 non-transparent 
watercolor paint. 
The pigment 
particles are 
large and 
the color vivid,
 which allows 
for a uniform 
coat of color.

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:09.370
Poster Color

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.470
 Bright Color

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:11.090
Vivid Tone.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:15.190
Hello! I am the little witch, Nodamiki!

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:19.470
With this rainbow brush I can make
anything bright and colorful in a flash.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:20.180
There!

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.480
My hair's been changed
 to this gaudy color!

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:27.490
My weak coarse tea has become
 the vivid green of fresh vegetables.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:38.000
<b> Colorless</b>

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:31.730
Natural, colorless, impurity-free white here!

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:33.550
Would you like some?

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:34.850
Oh! Thank you!

00:08:34.850 --> 00:08:37.460
I was getting so thirsty using all that magic!

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:38.130
Gulp.

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:40.330
What's happening?

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:43.370
After drinking white, 
my color has faded noda!

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:46.800
I can't call myself colorful anymore noda!

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.110
Stop ending everything with “Noda."

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.960
<b> Pastel</b>

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.960
 Dry art material 
made from 
powdered pigment 
and adhesive.
By shaving into 
powder or smudging 
with a finger a 
multitude of 
expressions can 
be effected.
Since pastels cannot 
be mixed, there 
are a large number
 of colors available.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:50.970
Pastel

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.280
 A light color

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:52.660
Pale Tone

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:57.230
Though I've got white mixed in, I'm still the little witch, Nodamiki!

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:58.420
With this pastel tone-

00:08:58.420 --> 00:08:59.350
That's enough!

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:00.690
So annoying!

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:03.150
<b> Colorful</b>

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.960
The chroma referred to as pastel color,

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:07.910
<b>Colorful => Pastel</b>

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:07.930
is indicated by a whitish, soft impression.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:14.930
 All white
Incomplete

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.440
Therefore, when you lecture us...

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.720
please do it in a pastel tone!

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:14.930
Softly!

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:19.440
<b> Hard Pastel 
(Hard type)</b>

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:19.440
<b> Oil Pastel
 (Oily and moist)</b>

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:19.440
Would you prefer the hard pastel or the oil pastel?

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:22.760
There are different kinds?

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:25.440
<b> Soft Type</b>

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:25.440
There's also what is known as Soft Pastel.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.860
<b>Oil Paint</b>

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.860
 Oil-based paint
 is made from
 a mixture of 
oil and pigment. 
The paint is 
usually applied 
in numerous 
layers.
 Often used in 
western art.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.010
Oil Paint

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:30.430
 A dull color

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:29.790
Dull tone.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:32.820
Second year Fine Arts Club member Homura-kun!

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:34.550
Go on, paint an oil painting!

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.590
What? I've never done one before!

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:39.090
I have no idea what to do with which tools!

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.010
The newbie is in trouble!

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.250
What's in this bottle! It stinks!

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:47.100
Aa-san, that's not how you treat underclassmen.

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:50.880
Do you often do oil paintings in GA?

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:53.580
Not really, in my classes
 we haven't done much.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.760
It takes a lot of time to
 create and to clean up,

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:57.380
and the materials are expensive, too.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:58.940
Hey, Buchi-san.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:01.060
you don't use water in oil painting, right?

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:03.650
How are you supposed to
 wash the brush and pallet?

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:07.650
I guess there are non-beginners
 who get in trouble as well.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:10.010
<b>Ink</b>

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:10.010
 A liquid made 
from mixing pigment 
and dyes. 
Used for coloring 
and drafting. 
The color is 
transparent 
and beautiful. 
When used for 
coloring, it is 
diluted with water.

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.320
Ink

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.660
Dark Color

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.110
Dark Tone

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:21.920
 Shhhhhhh

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:17.590
In contrast with the pastel page earlier...

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:20.050
What a heavy atmosphere...

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.930
Kyouju's blended in.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:29.440
<b> Light</b>

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:29.440
<b>Heavy</b>

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:25.710
Dark colors have low 
brightness and appear heavy.

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:29.440
On the other hand, high brightness
 evokes a lighter impression.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:32.420
For example, they say that if 
the ceiling of a room is dark,

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:35.070
the air seems heavy and
 it usually feels uneasy.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.630
But in the reverse,
 if the floor is dark

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:39.260
then your footing seems 
more solid, which is reassuring.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:41.230
So the reason why Namiko-san has

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:43.260
never worn her deep red jacket...

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:46.460
Could be because of her girlish 
desires to avoid seeming heavy!

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:48.280
Let's keep it to ourselves.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:51.450
<b>Transparent Watercolor</b>

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:51.450
 Transparent watercolor 
paint is made from 
a combination of pigment, 
water, and gum arabic. 
Since the pigment
 particles are small,
 the saturation can
 be adjusted through 
water dilution and 
it's a very transparent
 type of paint.
 It comes as a solid 
or in a tube.

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:51.850
Transparent watercolor

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:53.960
 Gray-ish

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:53.570
Grayish Tone

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:57.310
A gray sky and a gray toned uniform.

00:10:57.310 --> 00:11:00.460
Low saturation evokes a 
mature and grounded feeling.

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:03.940
For example, a party 
scene with little color.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:06.980
I get a sort of strange
 feeling of sadness.

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:10.160
Fruit and children's candy are the opposite.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:12.980
The greater the saturation,
 the more delicious they seem.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:16.250
On the other hand, 
the greater the color saturation,

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:20.200
the more you'll be suspicious of artificial 
coloring and unnatural ingredients.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.390
What a complicated world we live in.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.810
<b>Colored pencil</b>

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.810
 A coloring pencil 
is made from 
lead with added 
pigmentation. 
The lead is softer
than stationery
 pencils.
 Sometimes called
 oil-based pencils 
to differentiate
 from watercolor 
pencils.

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:25.240
Colored pencil

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:27.400
A strong color

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:27.000
Strong tone.

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:30.790
Hey, President, what art materials
 are best suited for a beginner?

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.470
Something not too tedious.

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:34.410
That would probably be colored pencils.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:37.020
Oh, those things.
 How many colors were in your set,

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.040
<b>12 Colors</b>

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:39.400
determined your social
 status in elementary school.

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:43.550
I wonder if there's a reason why 
they increase in increments of 12.

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:41.180
<b>24 Colors</b>

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.550
<b>48 Colors</b>

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:46.100
There are even color pencils that behave like

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:47.610
watercolors when used with water,

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:49.690
and, since your hands don't get messy,

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:51.410
you can take them outdoors to sketch.

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:53.950
Even after using them this much,

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:57.150
it looks like the white is still 
as long as it was to begin with.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:00.830
Yeah, you can never really find an 
opportunity to use that guy, can you?

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:03.230
<b>Charcoal</b>

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:03.230
 Made from 
charcoaled 
willow,
 chestnut,
 or mulberry 
branches. 
A special
 rough paper
 known as 
charcoal paper
 is used for
 charcoal 
sketching.

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:03.570
Charcoal

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:05.840
Single Color

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:05.520
Mono Tone

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:09.920
Do you really use white bread as 
an eraser in charcoal sketching?

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.900
Oh, yeah, we do.

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:15.810
I sure get asked that a lot by
 people who don't study art.

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:17.850
Why sliced white bread?

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:20.230
Are buns or bread rolls no good?

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:23.010
Well, probably because white bread is the cheapest.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:24.440
Otherwise it's just wasteful.

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:27.130
Oh, but you couldn't use oily bread.

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:29.720
Of course, you eat while you draw, right?

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.290
At first, yeah.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:33.010
But your hand turns completely black

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:34.380
when you do charcoal sketching...

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:37.100
Then the bread starts to 
dry out over time and harden.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:40.140
That's fine!
 You can still eat it.

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:43.140
Just think of it as slightly burnt toast.

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:45.120
What kind of mentality is that?

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.680
And in the end, we only really 
talked about bread the whole time.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:50.150
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:55.150
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:51.670
Glasses?

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:52.270
Round glasses.

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:53.770
Gotta be glasses.

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:02.330
I'm definitely going to fall 
asleep in class after lunch.

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:05.010
Then, how about I wake you
 up if you start to doze off?

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:07.040
Please...

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:08.830
Don't overdo it.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:11.490
Surrealism.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:15.840
In other words, hyper-realism,
 was introduced in the 20th century.

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:17.570
<b> Whack!</b>

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:20.600
The movement borrows its roots from the

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:20.030
What was the sound just now?

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:21.980
What? She won't wake up.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:24.580
desires and dreams thought to lie at the depths of the human heart...

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:24.580
Maybe you put her into a different kind of sleep.

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:28.380
...portraying a world beyond the scope of reality...

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:28.380
So then, Kyouju-san, if you please...

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:29.090
Understood.

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:32.760
Techniques including depaysement,

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:35.980
automatism, frottage

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:39.100
and decalcomania, were invented one after another.

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:40.570
Ouch!

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:42.770
What's going on over there?

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.680
Surrealism.

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:49.370
An artistic movement which began

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:53.650
with Andre Burton's declaration of surrealism in 1920.

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:53.650
Really? She's completely asleep.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:57.650
Its effects were wide spread, resulting in

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.450
Kisaragi, Kisaragi!

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:57.650
C'mon, wake up!

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:01.060
aesthetic changes in literature, art, photography, and film.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.060
What do we do? 
She won't wake up at all.

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:02.830
Very good.

00:14:01.510 --> 00:14:03.530
Kisaragi-chan, wake-up!

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:06.290
Next, Yamaguchi-san, please read from “As exemplified in...”

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:12.300
Y-yes!

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:13.960
As exemplified in De Chirico's 
metaphysical paintings,

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:20.300
<b> ZZZzzzz</b>

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:17.060
the stress was not on
 common knowledge or logic,

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:20.300
but rather on the unconscious or chance.

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:19.630
Keep it up, Tomokane!

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:22.810
Really? Is that what happened?

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.810
Don't you remember?

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:27.850
You were completely sound asleep.

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:29.030
I'm sorry.

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:32.820
After meals or PE I just get so weak...

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:35.320
It'd be nice if they had a class called "nap time."

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.920
Well, it's only two more hours of struggle.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.940
Why don't you do something
 to wake yourself up?

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:42.110
Yeah, like take a walk in 
the corridor or something.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.150
You're right.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:44.160
I'll do just that.

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:45.300
On the way, could you grab

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:47.080
some non-transparent 
watercolors from the lockers?

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:47.910
Here, the key.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:49.730
I'll take a set of brushes.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:52.210
Kisaragi, you're allowed to refuse.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:00.640
Wow, it's really raining.

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:03.080
No wonder the hallway seemed so dark.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:05.580
 Noda Miki

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:04.440
And, ah! Here it is.

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:05.580
Noda-chan.

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:08.980
Let's see. Watercolors. 
I think she wanted the transparent kind.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:09.350
<b> Sploosh</b>

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:12.240
Ahh! What! Wha! What!

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:14.260
W- w- w- what should I do?

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:16.790
Hey, Kisaragi!

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.470
I was worried, so I came to check on you.

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:22.300
Are you all right?

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:23.800
Can you swim?

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:25.950
Huh? Oh, y-yes.

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:27.310
If it's around 50 meters.

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:29.980
Oh okay! That's good.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:33.180
The truth is, this panel only seats one.

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:35.780
What? Tomokane-san!

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:43.720
Ya!

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:46.560
Red color scheme, 
blue color scheme, yellow color scheme!

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:48.250
Now you say it three times!

00:15:55.570 --> 00:15:57.450
What? Nobody's here.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:03.650
I wonder where everyone went.

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:33.300
Huh?

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:55.210
So you're awake, Kisaragi-dono?

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:56.730
What a surprise.

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:58.440
Oh, and she's tearing up.

00:16:58.440 --> 00:16:59.200
What happened?

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:00.850
Did you have a scary dream?

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:03.030
I thought so, but...

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:05.750
Why don't you do something
 to wake yourself up?

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.930
Yeah, like take a walk in 
the corridor or something.

00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:09.020
You're right.

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:10.040
I'll do just that.

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:11.190
On the way, could you grab

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:12.890
some non-transparent
 watercolors from the lockers?

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:13.900
Here, the key.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:15.810
I'll take a set of brushes.

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:21.820
I feel like this isn't the 
first time this has happened...

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:24.820
Well, whatever.

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:27.020
Oh, here it is!

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:29.830
I think Noda-chan asked 
for non-transparent watercolors.

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:34.250
And I got Tomokane-san's brushes as well.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.910
I'd better hurry back to the art room.

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:17.820
Huh?

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.130
What's wrong Kisa-chan?

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:22.700
Well, I was on my way 
back to the art room, but...

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.120
Did you get lost?

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:26.530
Huh? But if you have those with you,

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:27.620
then you should be able to get out right away.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:29.620
Those? What?

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:30.860
Those tools.

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:32.320
Let me see them for a second.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.630
Okay! It's done!

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:40.410
If you can't find it, you only have to paint it.

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:43.130
Let's see, was the fine art club's door like this?

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:45.990
What? Wha? 
But it's a picture!

00:18:45.990 --> 00:18:47.640
There, there. Off you go!

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:50.140
Huh? Outside...?

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:53.410
Why?

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:55.110
Hey, Kisaragi!

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.320
Namiko-san!

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:58.490
I'm about to fall... help me.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:00.120
But... in the middle of the air?

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:04.860
Namiko-san!

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:06.880
Ouch...

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:07.970
Are you okay?

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:10.250
What were you doing just now?

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:11.850
Oh, I was painting the sky.

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:13.060
Huh? The sky?!

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:15.910
I'm always painting that area of the sky.

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:17.200
It's my part time job, after all.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:18.070
Part time...?

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:20.550
But it's almost sunset.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:22.580
We'd better change the sky to night.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:26.410
Oh. It looks like I didn't bring enough black.

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:29.300
Oh dear.
 Kisaragi, do you have any black?

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:32.280
Oh, yes. I have Noda-chan's 
non-transparent watercolor.

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:33.920
But will that even help?

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:37.250
It doesn't look like it's been used before.

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:38.660
I wonder if it's okay to just open it—

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:42.430
Oh! Is that black brand new?

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:45.260
Paint that has been freshly uncapped is always lively.

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:46.430
Isn't it cute?

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:47.770
Didn't you know?

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:49.770
This is the first time I've heard of it!

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:55.530
The black color seems to have 
taken a liking to you, Kisaragi-dono.

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:57.760
Isn't that great, Kisaragi?

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:05.220
This is a dream...

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.610
Surely a dream...

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:09.720
Wake up, me!

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:24.480
Huh? These drawings are...

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:36.660
Me?

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:43.510
Oh? She finally woke up.

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:45.440
Good morning, Kisaragi-chan.

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:46.820
Do you know where this is?

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:48.860
Oh, huh?

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:50.660
You must have been really tired.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:53.120
Didn't you notice being carried to your seat?

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:55.400
There are two more hours,
 but are you going to be okay?

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:59.350
Yes. I'll go on a walk to wake myself up.

00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:02.740
Oh, and Noda-chan, Tomokane-san, 
I'll get your stuff along the way.

00:21:02.930 --> 00:21:04.650
Will you give me your keys?

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:05.510
What?!

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:06.510
How did you know?

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:07.800
E-ESPer!

00:21:08.380 --> 00:21:10.990
This week's assignment is really difficult!

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:14.350
I kinda feel like I get it...

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:17.990
Like those weird funky 
pieces you see in museums.

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:19.370
Here's your paint.

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:20.480
Thank you!

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:22.530
What's the assignment?

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:26.000
Oh, while you were sleeping, I
 put the handout in your sketchbook.

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:29.000
GA Year 1
 Assignment
Surrealism
 Magic Realism

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:29.000
We've been talking about how difficult it is.

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:31.300
It's about surrealism,

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:34.270
but we're in trouble because
 we can't explain it well.

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:36.510
Kisaragi-chan, what do you think it is?

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:39.780
Well, I suppose...

00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:54.250
It might be something like painting
 the world of your dreams.

00:23:25.130 --> 00:23:40.960
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:30.190
Whoa! The wind was so incredibly 
strong it blew Noda away!

00:23:30.190 --> 00:23:31.630
No, I'm fine!

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:33.860
Because Namiko-san was my stone weight!

00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:35.520
Noda, come here for a second.

00:23:35.520 --> 00:23:36.880
Kyouju-san, it's your turn.

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:40.960
Strong Wind Stories

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:39.620
Yes. If you're okay with me, 
then I will do my best.
